{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "TOKYO DRIVE",
    "steam_appid": 2954240,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >TOKYO DRIVE is a racing game that uses the location information (*) of actual roads and buildings in Tokyo, Japan (Tokyo's 23 wards).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is about enjoying driving a car on an open-world map that reproduces (*) the location of real roads.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Features]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Most of the roads in Tokyo (Tokyo's 23 wards) are reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Let's drive on the roads of the vast Tokyo Metropolis (Tokyo's 23 wards) (about 600 square kilometers).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fast travel function is available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Car purchase and transfer functions are available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is a collection element.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Day and night cycle (morning to night) is available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You may become familiar with places and roads in Tokyo (23 wards of Tokyo).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Can be played on non-high spec PCs.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(Can be played with on-board graphics (integrated graphics)).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Reproduction of roads and buildings] (*)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bridges (including overpasses) are not reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The elevation (topography) where roads and buildings are located is not reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(All roads are flat.) (Since there are many cities and few mountainous areas, there are no plans to support this feature at this time.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(The size of buildings is as close to the actual size as possible.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The location, size, and names of roads and buildings are current as of the time of positioning and may differ from the latest information.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The appearance of roads, ground, and buildings are automatically set and may differ from the actual ones.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u3000(Only the location and size of roads and buildings are reproduced.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The names of the buildings are mainly public institutions information on the in-game map. (Schools, stations, police stations, fire stations, post offices, etc.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(*)Information from MLIT Japan's Project PLATEAU is used.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Remarks]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We are planning to add various functions and improvements in the future. Please check the Early Access information in the store for details.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Please also refer to the Community Hub's Q&amp;A for current developments. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The author is not responsible for any disadvantages caused by the use of this game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >    (For example, the author cannot be held responsible if the road information is out of date.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u3000  ) Also, since the game contains a huge amount of road information, it requires several tens of gigabytes of space when installed, so please make sure you have enough free space to play.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >TOKYO DRIVE is a racing game that uses the location information (*) of actual roads and buildings in Tokyo, Japan (Tokyo's 23 wards).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is about enjoying driving a car on an open-world map that reproduces (*) the location of real roads.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Features]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Most of the roads in Tokyo (Tokyo's 23 wards) are reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Let's drive on the roads of the vast Tokyo Metropolis (Tokyo's 23 wards) (about 600 square kilometers).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fast travel function is available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Car purchase and transfer functions are available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is a collection element.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Day and night cycle (morning to night) is available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You may become familiar with places and roads in Tokyo (23 wards of Tokyo).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Can be played on non-high spec PCs.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(Can be played with on-board graphics (integrated graphics)).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Reproduction of roads and buildings] (*)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bridges (including overpasses) are not reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The elevation (topography) where roads and buildings are located is not reproduced.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(All roads are flat.) (Since there are many cities and few mountainous areas, there are no plans to support this feature at this time.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(The size of buildings is as close to the actual size as possible.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The location, size, and names of roads and buildings are current as of the time of positioning and may differ from the latest information.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The appearance of roads, ground, and buildings are automatically set and may differ from the actual ones.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u3000(Only the location and size of roads and buildings are reproduced.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The names of the buildings are mainly public institutions information on the in-game map. (Schools, stations, police stations, fire stations, post offices, etc.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(*)Information from MLIT Japan's Project PLATEAU is used.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Remarks]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We are planning to add various functions and improvements in the future. Please check the Early Access information in the store for details.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Please also refer to the Community Hub's Q&amp;A for current developments. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The author is not responsible for any disadvantages caused by the use of this game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >    (For example, the author cannot be held responsible if the road information is out of date.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u3000  ) Also, since the game contains a huge amount of road information, it requires several tens of gigabytes of space when installed, so please make sure you have enough free space to play.</p>",
